clk: imx8mp: keep the NAND/uSDHC bus clock running

uSDHC3 (the on-board eMMC) is driven by OP-TEE from the secure world and
is disabled in the Linux device tree, so from Linux's point of view the
shared nand_usdhc_bus root has no user whenever the SD card controller is
runtime-suspended, and the clock framework switches it off. That stalls
the data path of the secure-world controller mid-transfer. Mark the root
critical: the bus feeds a controller Linux does not manage.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board configuration for the TEE-owned eMMC]

--- a/drivers/clk/imx/clk-imx8mp.c	2026-09-15 13:47:02.424668183 +0000
+++ b/drivers/clk/imx/clk-imx8mp.c	2026-09-15 13:47:02.456668135 +0000
@@ -565,7 +565,8 @@
 
 	hws[IMX8MP_CLK_MAIN_AXI] = imx8m_clk_hw_composite_bus_critical("main_axi", imx8mp_main_axi_sels, ccm_base + 0x8800);
 	hws[IMX8MP_CLK_ENET_AXI] = imx8m_clk_hw_composite_bus("enet_axi", imx8mp_enet_axi_sels, ccm_base + 0x8880);
-	hws[IMX8MP_CLK_NAND_USDHC_BUS] = imx8m_clk_hw_composite("nand_usdhc_bus", imx8mp_nand_usdhc_sels, ccm_base + 0x8900);
+	/* Also feeds uSDHC3, which OP-TEE owns (RPMB): never let it be switched off */
+	hws[IMX8MP_CLK_NAND_USDHC_BUS] = imx8m_clk_hw_composite_critical("nand_usdhc_bus", imx8mp_nand_usdhc_sels, ccm_base + 0x8900);
 	hws[IMX8MP_CLK_VPU_BUS] = imx8m_clk_hw_composite_bus("vpu_bus", imx8mp_vpu_bus_sels, ccm_base + 0x8980);
 	hws[IMX8MP_CLK_MEDIA_AXI] = imx8m_clk_hw_composite_bus("media_axi", imx8mp_media_axi_sels, ccm_base + 0x8a00);
 	hws[IMX8MP_CLK_MEDIA_APB] = imx8m_clk_hw_composite_bus("media_apb", imx8mp_media_apb_sels, ccm_base + 0x8a80);
